    mq_min_coverage: "MIN. COVERAGE",
    mq_min_coverage_any: "every position",
    mq_min_coverage_help: "This pool carries every generic position; nothing has been selected for you. Coverage is how many receptors define the position at all — 3x50 exists in almost all of them, a bulge position such as 5x461 in a minority. The threshold limits which positions are offered; a position named in the query is still scored even if it falls below it.",
    mq_site_class: "BINDING SITE CLASS",
    mq_site_class_help: "Contact frequency is read within one class of binding site at a time, because the classes answer different questions: the canonical 7TM pocket is where a small molecule sits, the extracellular polymer interface is where a peptide lands on the surface. The number beside each is how many receptors in the atlas have a ligand of that class. The pool itself is the union over every class, so switching this changes which positions are offered, never which exist.",
    mq_min_freq: "MINIMUM FREQUENCY",
    mq_min_freq_help: "How often a position must contact a ligand to be offered: the share of that class's ligand-bound receptors in which it is within 4.5 Å of a ligand heavy atom. Counted per receptor, not per structure, so a receptor with eighty depositions counts once. Lowering it offers positions that matter to a few receptors; raising it keeps only what most of the class shares.",
