    mq_bw_translated: "Read as Ballesteros-Weinstein and translated: {pairs}",
    mq_bw_diverges: "The two numbering schemes disagree here: Ballesteros-Weinstein calls this {bw}, GPCRdb's structure-based scheme calls it {structure}. The atlas stores the structure-based number, so a position typed from a paper needs converting — which is what the label to the left shows, in GPCRdb's combined form.",
    mq_bw_diverges_variable: "The two numbering schemes disagree here, and not in the same way for every receptor. Ballesteros-Weinstein calls this {bw} in {n} of {total} receptors; elsewhere it is {variants}. GPCRdb's structure-based scheme calls it {structure} in all of them, which is why the atlas stores that one.",
    mq_bw_variable: "The Ballesteros-Weinstein number is not the same in every receptor: {bw} holds for {n} of {total}. A bulge one receptor has and another does not shifts every number above it.",
    mq_bw_minority: "The two schemes agree here for most receptors but not all: Ballesteros-Weinstein calls this {bw} in {n} of {total}, and something else in the other {share}% — {variants}. A bulge one receptor has and another does not shifts every number above it, so a position can be safe to read in one family and misleading in the next.",
