    sim_compare_open: "Compare structures", sim_compare_query: "Your query",
    sim_compare_shared: "The highlighted part is the ring system the two molecules share (the Bemis\u2013Murcko scaffold). It is shown because it is the common structure that can be computed in the browser, not because rings matter more. The score comes from the fingerprint of the whole molecule; similarity outside the rings does not appear in the highlight. Nor does the size of the highlight indicate the score: a shared scaffold can cover most of both molecules while the score stays low.",
    sim_compare_none: "The hit's whole ring framework — its Bemis–Murcko scaffold — was not found in the query. That does not mean the two share no rings: the individual rings and groups they share are listed in the enlarged view.",
    sim_scaffold_present: "The “shared ring system” option marks the Bemis–Murcko scaffold the two molecules share: the ring system with the side chains stripped.",
    sim_scaffold_absent: "There is no “shared ring system” option, because the hit's whole Bemis–Murcko scaffold was not found in the query. That does not mean the two share no rings: the rings they do share are listed individually above.",
